WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.195
Learning is not the same thing as exposure.

2
00:00:03.195 --> 00:00:12.380
A person can sit through a lesson, read a procedure, or watch a demonstration and still be unable to use the idea later.

3
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.971
In practical terms, learning means a durable change in understanding, skill, judgment, or behavior.

4
00:00:17.971 --> 00:00:23.562
Something has changed in what the learner can explain, decide, notice, perform, or improve.

5
00:00:23.562 --> 00:00:31.549
That difference matters because many training programs accidentally measure attendance, completion, or familiarity when the real goal is usable capability.

6
00:00:31.549 --> 00:00:33.545
There are levels of progress.

7
00:00:33.545 --> 00:00:36.740
Exposure means the learner has encountered the idea.

8
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.136
Familiarity means the idea feels recognizable.

9
00:00:39.136 --> 00:00:43.130
Recall means the learner can bring information back from memory.

10
00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:53.114
Usable capability means the learner can apply the idea in a real situation, with the normal messiness of time pressure, incomplete information, and competing priorities.

11
00:00:53.114 --> 00:01:01.101
A course that only tells people what to know may create familiarity, but it rarely creates confident performance by itself.

12
00:01:01.101 --> 00:01:02.698
Effective learning is active.

13
00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:12.682
People pay attention, connect new information to what they already know, form meaning, practice, receive feedback, adjust, and try again in a slightly different context.

14
00:01:12.682 --> 00:01:20.269
Good learning design starts with the work people need to do, not just the information they need to hear.

15
00:01:20.269 --> 00:01:32.649
When the desired performance is clear, the lesson can focus attention on the important relationships, give learners enough practice to build confidence, and help them transfer the skill beyond the course.

16
00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:39.039
A useful test is to ask what evidence would prove the learner can do the thing.

17
00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:45.428
If the outcome is only, they heard the message, the design will usually stop too early.

18
00:01:45.428 --> 00:01:57.409
If the outcome is, they can recognize a situation, choose an approach, explain a tradeoff, or complete a task, the course needs examples and practice that let those behaviors appear.
